course: dictionary
lesson: 4560
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Hebrews» can name a group of ancient people, a book in the Bible, or a language. Context tells you which meaning is right.
explain: Look for clues. In «Hebrews 11:31 and James 2:25 praise Rahab's faith and action in hiding the spies, not the lie as such; Christians have debated it since Augustine.», the numbers 11:31 and 2:25 are chapter and verse numbers, and James is another Bible book. Those clues show that Hebrews is a book here, not a people.
explain: Swap in your meaning to check. «The ancient people 11:31» does not make sense, but «the Letter to the Hebrews 11:31» does. Always test the meaning in the sentence before you decide.
fact: «Hebrews» with a capital H is a proper noun, because it names a special group, book or language.
fact: «The Hebrews» means the ancient people of Israel, the people of Abraham, Isaac, Jacob and Moses.
fact: «Hebrews» is also the name of a letter in the New Testament of the Bible.
fact: «Hebrew» is the language of the Jewish people and of modern Israel.
fact: Bible references such as 11:31 mean chapter 11, verse 31, so they often point to a book name.
exercise: «Hebrews 11:31 and James 2:25 praise Rahab's faith and action in hiding the spies.» In this sentence, Hebrews means which of these? | The language of modern Israel | A group of Bible readers | The ancient people of Israel | *The name of a letter in the New Testament
exercise: In lessons about the Hebrews in Egypt and the Exodus, what does Hebrews mean? | A type of Bible letter | The language of Egypt | *The ancient people of Israel | A modern country
exercise: «Hebrew is also the language of the Jewish people and of modern Israel.» What is Hebrew in this sentence? | A town | A letter | *A language | A person's name
test: «A reading from the Letter to the Hebrews» is heard in church. What does Hebrews mean here? | A place to pray | *A book of the Bible | A language | A people
test: Which clue shows that Hebrews is a book in «Hebrews 11:31 and James 2:25 praise Rahab's faith»? | The word Christians | The word praise | The word spies | *The numbers 11:31 and 2:25
exam: Which meaning fits «The Hebrews were the people of Abraham and Moses»? | *A people | A letter | A town | A language
